Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.610 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  the division 2 is almost here and those  of you who played the beta will probably  already know that several things feel  similar to the division 1 that said  there are a few really interesting new  features that we discovered from the  beta which are primed to spice things up  this time around it may be the post  apocalypse but that doesn't mean there  aren't plenty of survivors and ways to  help them in the division - this is  emphasized through settlements  settlements include plenty of NPCs who  need your help opportunities for side  quests and projects to undertake which  will grant you with blueprints and other  goodies if you can rustle up certain  supplies and bring them back settlements  also offer up new traders and  recruitable NPCs for the White House  base which provides access to new items  and perks the inclusion of projects also  makes chasing collectables feel more  rewarding not to mention the warm  fuzzies from everyone telling you you're  awesome when you bolster your  settlements and White House headquarters  [Music]  there's enough of an endgame revamp in  the division to that you really need to  check out our in-depth preview innocence  though the game has been developed with  endgame in mind from the very beginning  the hallmarks of the experience are the  new high ranking specializations that  come with power weapons and invaded  missions which feature the same mission  areas as earlier in the game but they're  now occupied by a brutally tough new  faction called the black tusk  this comes hand-in-hand with the new  occupied dark zone an area under black  tusk occupation that ignores level  balancing and friendly fire handicaps  but has great rewards for those who can  handle it characters are also far more  personalized and customizable this time  around with multiple types for each  gadget plenty of mods and an overall  deeper skill set  much like the endgame there's a lot of  new bits and pieces to check out in the  dark zone but one of the most welcomed  changes is that you don't feel like  you've wasted time if you're killed off  at loot extraction as division 1 players  can attest nothing is worse than sinking  an hour into the dark zone only to lose  your loot at the last second now you can  pick up uncontaminated loot which you'll  be able to keep and use without having  to extract it first contaminated loot  can still be found and extracted but it  will be reserved for rarer gear on top  of that there are new rewards for those  who are keen to go rogue as you'll open  up access to unique vendors throughout  the dark zone  while I personally enjoyed the concrete  jungle of New York City there's a lot to  be said for the shift over to Washington  there are more varied environments than  before not to mention both greenery and  critters like deer and raccoons running  amuck the bay that didn't provide access  to the entire map but what we've seen so  far is promising patrolling friendlies  add a new element to open world  exploration maintaining ownership of  control points scattered around the  capital opens up access to supply rooms  full of loot and having the White House  as your base of operations to defend and  rebuild is just super cool there's also  a greater focus on visiting landmarks  and even a mission to steal the  Declaration of Independence  so you're basically Nic Cage  one of the more frustrating aspects of  the division was the damn near  bulletproof enemies who you had to chip  away at to take down the division to  addresses the bullet sponge complaints  in a pretty interesting way weaker  enemies are fairly squishy and easy to  take down  while tougher foes have armor you'll  need to target before you go in for the  kill this means you'll want to be more  strategic about where you hit tough  enemies but once that armor is gone they  go down faster will you still be  emptying entire clips onto elite enemies  shop but at least you can see the fruits  of your labor this time around let me  know which of the division choose new  features you're most excited about down  in that comment box and stay tuned to  gave us what for the rest of our  coverage

